Subject: Re: simNmix visualization
Message-ID: <hdn5mD2H1Z0.DKE5o5PpAQAJ@hmecology.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <hdn5mD2H1Z0.qZBE8NYgBQAJ@hmecology.groups.google.com>
References: <hdn5mD2H1Z0.qZBE8NYgBQAJ@hmecology.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/hmecology/c/hdn5mD2H1Z0/m/DKE5o5PpAQAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi Wendy,

The analytical solution should be some sort of decay towards the true value of lambda rather than a polynomial-looking curve, I would think.  Fixing the df on the smoother is probably fine for visualizing the relationship, or not fixing the df but also not taking the humps too seriously.

